{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454226-thinbloods-messy-crits-and-bestial-failures","id":1454226,"title":"Thinbloods: Messy Crits and Bestial Failures?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-04T12:41:03-07:00","id":1454226,"title":"Thinbloods: Messy Crits and Bestial Failures?","content":"We know that thinbloods can't frenzy unless compelled to by magical means or if they take the appropriate flaw, but I want to say they are subject to bestial failures and messy crits. Is that accurate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T14:07:43-07:00","id":1454237,"title":"","content":"It looks like they are:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Hunger and Frenzy</b><br /> A thin-blood suffers hunger just as any vampire. However, the Beast is far less overt, and a thin-blood never frenzies unless provoked by supernatural means (such as Ani\u0002malism, p. 244).&quot;<br /> <br /> The heading refers to hunger as well as frenzy, even though it doesn't present any unique rules about hunger, besides hunger frenzies. Presumably bestial failures/messy criticals are how they &quot;suffer hunger just as any vampire&quot;. Furthermore, this says that they do have a Beast, but a less overt one and hunger rolls are less overt than frenzies.<br /> Suddenly, being a thin-blood sounds less appealing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T14:14:50-07:00","id":1454238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454226-thinbloods-messy-crits-and-bestial-failures?p=1454237#post1454237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like they are:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Hunger and Frenzy</b><br /> A thin-blood suffers hunger just as any vampire. However, the Beast is far less overt, and a thin-blood never frenzies unless provoked by supernatural means (such as Ani\u0002malism, p. 244).&quot;<br /> <br /> The heading refers to hunger as well as frenzy, even though it doesn't present any unique rules about hunger, besides hunger frenzies. Presumably bestial failures/messy criticals are how they &quot;suffer hunger just as any vampire&quot;. Furthermore, this says that they do have a Beast, but a less overt one and hunger rolls are less overt than frenzies.<br /> Suddenly, being a thin-blood sounds less appealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still comparatively better though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T18:17:22-07:00","id":1454316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454226-thinbloods-messy-crits-and-bestial-failures#post1454226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We know that thinbloods can't frenzy unless compelled to by magical means or if they take the appropriate flaw, but I want to say they are subject to bestial failures and messy crits. Is that accurate?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rules as written it IS accurate. More over frenzy is a serious issue full-bloods have to deal with, I personally think more so than what is portrayed in more live games on youtube. It is a complete loss of control. I think the duskborn can deal with being hangry haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T10:05:02-07:00","id":1454355,"title":"","content":"I house ruled it for my game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> same for lower gen... golden rule FTW <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8757-pram","name":"Pram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T16:09:52-07:00","id":1454387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454226-thinbloods-messy-crits-and-bestial-failures#post1454226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We know that thinbloods can't frenzy unless compelled to by magical means or if they take the appropriate flaw, but I want to say they are subject to bestial failures and messy crits. Is that accurate?</div> </div> </div> </div>They 100% suffer from Messy Crits and Bestial Failures. They just don't frenzy is the only major difference in this case. They however, can easily suffer from the more subtle aspects of the beast such as Compulsions and consequences of hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"